&lt;th&gt;Collections&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Highlights&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hackathon&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Events, Teams, Participants, Submissions, Judges, Scores&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Multi-lookup, filters, cross-references&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CRM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Companies, Contacts, Deals, Activities&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Lookups, related lists, stage filters&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Members, Projects, Milestones, Tasks&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Tree view, multi-lookup teams&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Catalog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Categories, Suppliers, Products, Parts&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Nested tree views, bill of materials&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product CMS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Pages, Products, Features&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Page hierarchy, content management&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Copy any JSON into your &lt;code&gt;datamodel.json&lt;/code&gt;, deploy, and you have a working app.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Get Started
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The full template is open source:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/nicheComposer/codehooks-io-templates/tree/main/react-admin-dashboard" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GitHub: react-admin-dashboard&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm i &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-g&lt;/span&gt; codehooks
coho create myapp &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--template&lt;/span&gt; react-admin-dashboard
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Five minutes from now, you could have a production admin dashboard running. No CRUD boilerplate. No auth plumbing. No form builders.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Describe what you need. Let AI write the JSON. Ship it.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;What would you build with this? I'm curious what datamodels people come up with. Drop your ideas in the comments.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
